Reading (inference): dynamic power does not follow die temperature, so the clock-dependent idle power D of a rail is at most the part of its idle law that does not follow temperature, P_fix. P_fix depends on the form of the leakage law (all three fit the 30 C span about equally):
  aifoundry3 minion: exp: rms 0.0370 W, P_fix 1.73 (band 1.23 .. 2.24) | arr: rms 0.0355 W, P_fix 3.20 (band 2.84 .. 3.53) | T2arr: rms 0.0356 W, P_fix 3.00 (band 2.61 .. 3.35)
  aifoundry3 sram  : exp: rms 0.0067 W, P_fix 0.29 (band -0.01 .. 0.29) | arr: rms 0.0063 W, P_fix 0.70 (band 0.63 .. 0.76) | T2arr: rms 0.0064 W, P_fix 0.69 (band 0.55 .. 0.75)
  aifoundry2 minion: exp: rms 0.0287 W, P_fix 0.58 (band -0.65 .. 1.80) | arr: rms 0.0283 W, P_fix 2.47 (band 0.96 .. 3.40) | T2arr: rms 0.0283 W, P_fix 2.20 (band 0.59 .. 3.40)
  aifoundry2 sram  : exp: rms 0.0091 W, P_fix -0.95 (band -1.97 .. -0.20) | arr: rms 0.0090 W, P_fix -0.26 (band -0.97 .. 0.14) | T2arr: rms 0.0090 W, P_fix -0.34 (band -1.11 .. 0.14)
=> bound on D at 600 MHz (union of the three forms): minion rail aifoundry3 <= 3.53 W, aifoundry2 <= 3.40 W; SRAM rail aifoundry3 <= 0.76 W, aifoundry2 <= 0.14 W
unmetered W per rail W (E46 fit, docs/reports/sources/limits-of-observability.data.json power.fit): aifoundry2 minion 0.188, SRAM 0.034, NoC 0.291; aifoundry3 minion 0.181, SRAM 0.043, NoC 0.294

