==============================================================================================================
C. A and B together: the voltage exponent of leakage (P_leak ~ V^n) and the clock-dependent idle power D
==============================================================================================================
idle rails at 600 MHz at 64 C (E51 idle samples): minion 8.58 W, SRAM 1.46 W; delivery loss k_minion 0.188, k_SRAM 0.034; SRAM D_s ~ U(0, 0.14) W
the relation the step fixes (median step, D_s = 0): D_m on aifoundry2 -> the leakage exponent n: 0.0 W -> 2.81, 0.5 W -> 2.76, 1.0 W -> 2.70, 1.5 W -> 2.64, 2.0 W -> 2.57, 2.5 W -> 2.49, 3.0 W -> 2.39, 3.5 W -> 2.28, 4.0 W -> 2.15
draws that reproduce the step with 0 <= D_m <= P_m: 24110 of 40000: n 1.09 / 1.91 / 2.71, D_m 0.896 / 4.68 / 6.06 W
... and also D_m <= 3.40 W (section A, aifoundry2, union of the forms): 6796: n 2.26 / 2.55 / 2.82 (2.5/50/97.5 %), D_m 0.164 / 2.15 / 3.35 W
=> registered leakage exponent band (inference from measured A and B): n in [2.26, 2.82], central 2.55. FinFET textbook (tools/claims-v3/nv/DESIGN.md s3): 1.5-2.4; DIBL-only with the O11 figures (40 mV/V, 65 mV/dec) at 0.52 V: 1.74
   leakage power factor minion 525 -> 400 mV: x0.465 .. x0.540 (central x0.500); under the rival band n 1.4 .. 2.26: x0.540 .. x0.683
   leakage power factor SRAM 700 -> 660 mV: x0.847 .. x0.875 (central x0.861); under the rival band n 1.4 .. 2.26: x0.875 .. x0.921
transferred to aifoundry3 (6796 joint draws): D_m 0.283 / 2.09 / 3.2 W, n 2.3 / 2.55 / 2.79
CROSS-PREDICTION (registered): the D_m that Stage A measures on aifoundry3 fixes the n that Stage B must find: 0.0 W -> n 2.81, 0.5 W -> n 2.76, 1.0 W -> n 2.70, 1.5 W -> n 2.64, 2.0 W -> n 2.56, 2.5 W -> n 2.48, 3.0 W -> n 2.38, 3.5 W -> n 2.26 (+-0.05 from the step's spread and the 0.92-0.99 transfer)

